  message: "Fixed in PR #1977 (d3bbf8bdcf). One PATH predicate (paths.classify_test_file absorbed is_test_path's shapes plus FooIT / *Test.scala / unittest/; filters.is_test_path is the same function), one NODE predicate (paths.is_test_node: path or test annotation, dict or text form), called by every node-level consumer: cli views (routes, explain/symbols -x, test-coverage, dead-code, repeat-finder, handler slices), sketch, compact, key-symbol / production-edge filters, ranking, entrypoints, receiver_blind_magnets, the test-only ratchet, symbol_resolution, six linkers; scripts/bakeoff-deep and hypergumbo_diag call the core predicates. Re-run on merged dev, live on ripgrep's default survey: dead-code-maybe 383 candidates, 0 of them test code (was 817, 434 tests); test-coverage 2,187 production functions, 0 test code (was 2,680, 493), total_tests 582 (was 89), coverage 36.2% (was 9.3%). mitmproxy, knex, logrus, jedis unchanged on both views; re-surveys: jedis identical, ripgrep 5 edges retargeted (production Box::new / err.path() no longer bound to a test-module TempDir helper). Residual, stated: the concept rule's two copies (cli dict closure, sketch _has_test_concept) are not merged; bakeoff-deep's bare integration/ and TestFoo prefix rules did not move into core, so those measurements narrow."  # f54b
